# Route Directus film images through Netlify's edge CDN [BF-107].
#
# MUST live in _redirects (not netlify.toml): Netlify processes _redirects
# rules BEFORE netlify.toml, and the Nitro Netlify preset emits a catch-all
# fallback here. Placing this rule in public/_redirects makes Nitro keep it
# ABOVE that fallback (see nitropack .../presets/netlify/utils.mjs), so /cms/*
# is proxied instead of falling through to the 404 handler.
#
# The origin sends cache-control: public,max-age=2592000 + last-modified, so
# Netlify caches each transformed image at its edge; only misses hit Directus.
# Query string (width/format/quality) is forwarded automatically.
/cms/*  https://bfna.simplyas.com/assets/:splat  200!
